}]={(i,k)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,{i}^{3}]}\n$$\n\nis the vertical line segment from the point $(i,0)$ to the point $(i,{i}^{3}).$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/472b6456019a5c89e585f80aa4a0dfd44f3b87c0624c10ea7b52f32e958a8c4e.png)\n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following figure that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/204c9a31031534ac70a599322c3f77a077440300fde2364476643c88406e34cd.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308037 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5793f07d-e0de-5707-a5e1-32d657244e0b" :knowledge-point/title "Visualizing Intersections of Uncountable Families of Indexed Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb34c5ca-e1ec-5bff-a6c1-dfefe7196dd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/236d10f31265b400036e1ddeafa122991bcae1ea878af8b300003fb11acfa85b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308039} {:answer/id #uuid "70ed1b78-a8f8-52f9-8f84-6fb39ffab773" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/5e474959f4172f2a3dc7d104a5b7e27a8eece4fc1f13421fefdfdfc2e139c139.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308040} {:answer/id #uuid "9ef4002b-12fd-55a6-b140-4b4496a21f07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/37de777f63941a62b003a4c600a40df648b3d39ce3c1dfc753c6f406fe230330.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308041} {:answer/id #uuid "6a36a47b-91e8-52db-859a-472192176ea0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/efb6d92ea0dc70fa0cbd9d82ea838b41a4eaab6ee2fc32c6fada9258a4154680.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308042} {:answer/id #uuid "f4968d13-0264-5929-ab6c-6780d8208be3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/47ee12b24246473a45e057d4da6dac5190a4eab23e18bb37bef494bf07627daa.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308043}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb34c5ca-e1ec-5bff-a6c1-dfefe7196dd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/236d10f31265b400036e1ddeafa122991bcae1ea878af8b300003fb11acfa85b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308039} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa70e261-3b80-5b2f-ac47-ee8c6eb9adeb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308038}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2f711893-9075-516f-888f-e39a0f91809d" :question/math-academy-id "q-184507" :question/problem "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[0,2]\\times [-i,0].$ Which of the following represents ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the intersection of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *all* the sets:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for all}\\,\\,k\\in I}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}=[0,2]\\times [-0.5,0]={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [0,2],b\\in [-0.5,0]}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a rectangle whose vertices are at $(0,0),$ $(2,0),$ $(2,-0.5),$ and $(0,-0.5)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/5837864bfcc40e680cf62b43c0e3d145ba05b1f25e1ccae2f4788902d030d927.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[0,2]\\times [-i,0]={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [0,2],b\\in [-i,0]}\n$$\n\nis the rectangle whose vertices are at $(0,0),$ $(2,0),$ $(2,-i),$ and $(0,-i).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/f0c20436f03db4b0003d087827cefbd76506af423da3f0a3042082b5afeb4b58.png)\n\nThe intersection of all these rectangles is the line segment $[0,2]\\times {0}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/236d10f31265b400036e1ddeafa122991bcae1ea878af8b300003fb11acfa85b.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308044 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5793f07d-e0de-5707-a5e1-32d657244e0b" :knowledge-point/title "Visualizing Intersections of Uncountable Families of Indexed Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31b313d8-3a87-5dcc-9a22-44962a5715d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/08ca3b1dd409fa953338c05f2089772ec78a0b64da1b131f82d6d9f02afd7c1e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308046} {:answer/id #uuid "d92cc473-f2a7-55bd-be6e-2a14743bd75a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/5d83de0d0c317ac7663e607f826251a541017464a8e0ffa7b4c322a0443f7781.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308047} {:answer/id #uuid "608c8d11-3de6-5c47-ba38-62796da1c502" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/581e4aec0613b738b5978db3f527ad481228a4610e0576930311115c190e0535.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308048} {:answer/id #uuid "0bb0fcd9-7f49-523d-bd44-c6847724eb30"