Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/0fef44c4b8c4911a892d7dad4502edbb80ef236553d6fddb57de1472bd44a62b.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[0,1]\\times [0,i]={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [0,1],b\\in [0,i]}\n$$\n\nis the rectangle whose vertices are at $(0,0),$ $(0,1),$ $(i,1),$ and $(i,0).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/f4602a46d3e4fc1799a475f05548ef278fdd33d354d1ec19ca4e5c5cc34cfcf8.png)\n\nThe intersection of all these rectangles is the line segments $[0,1]\\times {0}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/19a2cd951a55508269a0034aec582345bf7e350ec516fe1eecac0d6bf5847981.png)"}]}
